Ahoy, there be spoilers here...

So first of all, I'd like to say that the PYEC (Platinum Yendorian Express
Card) seems a bit unbalancing, overall.  

Polypiling with a wand of polymorph and the PYEC is *easier* than 
polypiling used to be, because you don't have to worry about where your next
charge is coming from.  This means that you can collect tools to polymorph
by using the wand on all those chests lying about.

Enchanting rings to the limit is also much easier, because the PYEC will
do it for you.  Of course, you may need to polypile to get a few more
rings to experiment on.  I've never seen a ring go past +8.

Finally, the PYEC + a horn of plenty = infinite food + potions

Admittedly, the potions are a bit more rare, but you can afford to wait for
and collect them (I mean...  It's not like you're going to starve to 
death...).  So...  Here's the abuse...  If you're *lucky* enough to have
smoky potions be fruit juice, just collect all that yummy fruit juice, bless
it, and drink it.  Eventually, you'll get a wish out of it.  Repeat until
you're stoked...  Of course, you could always polymorph those potions until
you get smoky ones and collect them that way...

So...  PYEC + wand of polymorph --> horn of plenty --> infinite wishes
(for the patient among us, anyway...)

